Below is a **step‑by‑step playbook** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, folder layouts, and tooling recommendations.  
Feel free to skip sections that already match your current setup.

---

## 1️⃣ Planning & Design

| What | Why | How |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Define core pages** | Product listing, product detail, cart, checkout, account, admin | Sketch a sitemap. |
| **Create wireframes** | Visualise layout before coding | Use Figma/Sketch/Adobe XD. |
| **Design a UI kit** | Consistent look & feel | Build a component library (React + Storybook). |
| **Accessibility audit** | WCAG 2.1 compliance | Use axe, Lighthouse. |
| **Performance goals** | Fast first paint, low CLS | Aim for < 2 s load, < 0.1 CLS. |

> **Tip:** Keep a shared design system (colors, typography, spacing) in a single source of truth (e.g., a `theme.ts` file).

---

## 2️⃣ Tech Stack Decision

| Category | Options | Recommendation |
|----------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React + Next.js** (SSR + SSG + ISR) |
| **State mgmt** | Redux, Zustand, Recoil, React‑Query | **Redux Toolkit + RTK Query** (or React‑Query if you prefer hooks) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Tailwind CSS | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **Type safety** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** |
| **Testing** | Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress | Jest + RTL for unit, Cypress for E2E |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | GitHub Actions (free for public repos) |
| **Hosting** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (great with Next.js) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Built‑in SSR/SSG for SEO.  
> • Image optimization (`next/image`).  
> • API routes for serverless functions (e.g., Stripe webhook).  
> • Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) for dynamic product pages.

---

## 3️⃣ Project Skeleton

```
my-ecommerce/
├─ public/
│  ├─ images/
│  └─ favicon.ico
├─ src/
│  ├─ components/
│  │  ├─ ui/          # UI primitives (Button, Card, Input)
│  │  ├─ layout/      # Header, Footer, Sidebar
│  │  └─ pages/       # Page‑specific components
│  ├─ pages/
│  │  ├─ api/         # Next.js API routes
│  │  ├─ _app.tsx
│  │  ├─ index.tsx
│  │  ├─ product/[slug].tsx
│  │  ├─ cart.tsx
│  │  ├─ checkout.tsx
│  │  └─ admin/
│  ├─ store/
│  │  ├─ slices/
│  │  ├─ api/
│  │  └─ store.ts
│  ├─ styles/
│  │  ├─ globals.css
│  │  └─ tailwind.css
│  ├─ utils/
│  │  ├─ api.ts
│  │  └─ helpers.ts
│  └─ types/
│     └─ index.d.ts
├─ .env.local
├─ .gitignore
├─ next.config.js
├─ package.json
└─ README.md
```

---

## 4️⃣ Core Components (React + Tailwind)

### 4.1 UI Primitive – Button

```tsx
// src/components/ui/Button.tsx
import { ButtonHTMLAttributes } from 'react';

export interface ButtonProps extends ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'outline';
}

export const Button = ({
  variant = 'primary',
  className,
  ...props
}: ButtonProps) => {
  const base = 'px-4 py-2 rounded font-medium focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2';
  const variants = {
    primary: 'bg-indigo-600 text-white hover:bg-indigo-700 focus:ring-indigo-500',
    secondary: 'bg-gray-600 text-white hover:bg-gray-700 focus:ring-gray-500',
    outline: 'border border-indigo-600 text-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-50 focus:ring-indigo-500',
  };

  return (
    <button
      className={`${base} ${variants[variant]} ${className}`}
      {...props}
    />
  );
};
```

### 4.2 Product Card

```tsx
// src/components/pages/ProductCard.tsx
import Image from 'next/image';
import Link from 'next/link';
import { Button } from '../ui/Button';

export interface ProductCardProps {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  imageUrl: string;
  slug: string;
}

export const ProductCard = ({
  id,
  title,
  price,
  imageUrl,
  slug,
}: ProductCardProps) => (
  <div className="border rounded overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
    <Link href={`/product/${slug}`}>
      <a>
        <Image
          src={imageUrl}
          alt={title}
          width={400}
          height={400}
          className="object-cover w-full h-64"
        />
      </a>
    </Link>
    <div className="p-4">
      <h3 className="font-semibold text-lg">{title}</h3>
      <p className="text-indigo-600 font-bold mt-2">${price.toFixed(2)}</p>
      <Button className="mt-4 w-full" onClick={() => console.log('Add to cart', id)}>
        Add to Cart
      </Button>
    </div>
  </div>
);
```

---

## 5️⃣ Data Layer – RTK Query

```ts
// src/store/api/products.ts
import { createApi, fetchBaseQuery } from '@reduxjs/toolkit/query/react';

export const productsApi = createApi({
  reducerPath: 'productsApi',
  baseQuery: fetchBaseQuery({ baseUrl: '/api' }),
  endpoints: (builder) => ({
    getProducts: builder.query<Product[], void>({
      query: () => 'products',
    }),
    getProductBySlug: builder.query<Product, string>({
      query: (slug) => `products/${slug}`,
    }),
  }),
});

export const { useGetProductsQuery, useGetProductBySlugQuery } = productsApi;
```

> **Tip:** Use `RTK Query` for caching, polling, and optimistic updates. It’s a drop‑in replacement for `React‑Query` if you’re already on Redux Toolkit.

---

## 6️⃣ Page Implementation

### 6.1 Product Listing (SSG)

```tsx
// src/pages/index.tsx
import { GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { useGetProductsQuery } from '../store/api/products';
import { ProductCard } from '../components/pages/ProductCard';

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async () => {
  // Fetch from your headless CMS or database
  const res = await fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/products`);
  const products = await res.json();
  return { props: { products }, revalidate: 60 }; // ISR
};

export default function Home({ products }) {
  return (
    <main className="container mx-auto p-4">
      <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Shop</h1>
      <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        {products.map((p) => (
          <ProductCard key={p.id} {...p} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </main>
  );
}
```

### 6.2 Product Detail (ISR)

```tsx
// src/pages/product/[slug].tsx
import { GetStaticPaths, GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { useGetProductBySlugQuery } from '../../store/api/products';
import Image from 'next/image';
import { Button } from '../../components/ui/Button';

export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {
  const res = await fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/products`);
  const products = await res.json();
  const paths = products.map((p) => ({ params: { slug: p.slug } }));
  return { paths, fallback: 'blocking' }; // ISR
};

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async ({ params }) => {
  const res = await fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/products/${params?.slug}`);
  const product = await res.json();
  return { props: { product }, revalidate: 60 };
};

export default function ProductPage({ product }) {
  return (
    <main className="container mx-auto p-4 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8">
      <Image src={product.imageUrl} alt={product.title} width={500} height={500} />
      <div>
        <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold">{product.title}</h1>
        <p className="text-2xl text-indigo-600 mt-2">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
        <p className="mt-4">{product.description}</p>
        <Button className="mt-6" onClick={() => console.log('Add to cart', product.id)}>
          Add to Cart
        </Button>
      </div>
    </main>
  );
}
```

